  "visualDNA": {
    "Façade lay-out": "Following the original, Renaissance Revival façades contain horizontal lines, for much of its length and often completely end-to-end. In a similar way both original and revival façades are finished with cornice.",
    "Staircase": "One of the most widely copied features of Renaissance architecture were the great staircases from the chateaux of Blois and Chambord. Blois had been the favourite residence of the French kings throughout the renaissance. The Francis I wing, completed in 1524,  of which the staircase is an integral part was one of the earliest examples of French Renaissance."
